Q what is flyway ?
Flyway is a database migration tool. It manages changes to your database schema over time in a controlled, versioned way.

  The problem it solves:

  When your app evolves, you need to create tables, add columns, change indexes etc. You can't just manually run SQL on every server — you'd lose track of what's been applied where.

  How it works:

  You write numbered SQL files called migrations:
  db/migration/
    V1__create_user_login.sql
    V2__add_email_index.sql
    V3__add_profile_table.sql

  On startup, Flyway checks which migrations have already run (it tracks this in a flyway_schema_history table) and runs any new ones automatically.

  In your case:

  Every time art-user-engine starts, Flyway runs before the app is ready. It connects to MySQL and applies any pending migration scripts — so your schema is always in sync with your code, without you doing anything manually.


